find: pruning an -xdev mount point must not end the walk of its siblings

walkdir's skip_current_dir() pops the directory it last entered. Under
-xdev it does not enter a directory on another file system, so -prune on
one popped the parent instead: `find / -xdev -path /proc -prune -o -name
sudoers -print` stopped listing / at /proc, printed nothing and exited 0.
Skip only a directory walkdir entered. GNU findutils prints /etc/sudoers.

Signed-off-by: Pat Wendorf <dungeons@gmail.com>
Upstream: not yet offered (no upstream fix or issue as of 2026-10-27)
